{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957340-advice-on-character-build","id":957340,"title":"Advice on character build","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-24T19:41:55-07:00","id":957340,"title":"Advice on character build","content":"Good evening.<br /> <br /> Recently i got an invitation to join a mix WoD party containing two Geists , one Changeling and 2 Mages. Since almost no one is combat focused i tried to make a &quot;killing machine&quot; but my Gm adviced me for something more &quot;Spirit specialist&quot; like a Bone shadow shaman etc.<br /> After a careful study on werewolf rites and gifts i came on the conclusion that our &quot;spells&quot; are little flashy magic comparing the Mages spells.... So my question is , is it worthy to make such a character in a mixed party or should i stay in my (almost) no brain killing machine.<br /> Take note that i will start with 180 exp and the setting is taking place in Gotham city.<br /> Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12328-prisonerx","user":"PrisonerX","date":". 08-24-2016, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12328-prisonerx","name":"PrisonerX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T20:07:09-07:00","id":957357,"title":"","content":"You can have a little bit of both worlds actually. If you want a &quot;killing machine&quot; but the ST wants you to be &quot;spirit specialist&quot;, then I recommend trying either a Rahu Bone Shadow or a Itheaur Blood Talon. You might find something to your liking somewhere between those two combos.<br /> <br /> It might help me and others if we knew a bit more about which edition rules you guys are using, and what the Mage players are going to be focusing on with their characters. Are any of them focusing on the Spirit Arcanum? If so, don't bother making a &quot;spirit specialist&quot;. It will out do anything your wolf can do and may serve to make you feel usless in the long run. Hope that helps a bit.<br /> <br /> Also, Gotham huh? I ran a Gotham based game awhile back. To date, it has been our most successful chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T20:23:24-07:00","id":957368,"title":"","content":"I would really suggest going Irraka or Rahu Bone Shadow. Even if the party mages aren't spirit specialists, if you go Ithaeur the first few Moon Gifts are going to be quickly outclassed by anyone who takes a dip into Spirit. Moon Gifts tend to be your most powerful ones so it would be better to get ones you would actually use. Full Moon Gifts are very warrior-like, with the first giving you an 8-again on all Brawl and Weaponry rolls for the scene, and the second a permanent extra Health based on your Renown. New Moon's first Gift is great, giving you really powerful ambushing attacks.<br /> <br /> From there the Bone Shadows would give you the 'spirit specialist,' with the Bottle Spirit rite and some large-scale spells like Read the World's Loom. Though with your Experiences you may want to drop a lot in Elemental Gifts, which are really fantastic with high Renown. You can have some mystical might while still having the Rahu or Irraka access to ass-kicking Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T20:24:52-07:00","id":957369,"title":"","content":"My apologies, we run under the first edition rules, our mages are both focused on Time, space and life arcanas. As we talked they are not interested on spirit arcana.<br /> Gotham has a natural horror feeling ,it is great indeed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12328-prisonerx","name":"PrisonerX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T20:40:57-07:00","id":957375,"title":"","content":"Oh, first edition, with first edition mages and sin-eaters. I love the game, but first edition had some problems.<br /> <br /> In that case I think I would suggest an Ithaeur Auspice, with an emphasis on the Witch's Moon Gifts, and Storm Lord or Blood Talon for Tribe. That would be for a spirit specialist who could fight.<br /> <br /> You might look over these pages on the WodCodex. There's <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Gifts_(1st_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">one for Gifts</a> and <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Rites_(1st_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">one for Rites</a>, offering brief descriptions of them and what pages in which books you can find them in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T05:40:18-07:00","id":958166,"title":"","content":"If you use Signs of the Moon, I'd go for Ithaeur (Storm Lord, Lodge of Winter, because they are cool), and bump up the Gifts of Wisdom, because they are useful not only for you, but in a buffing capacity for the whole party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T17:12:45-07:00","id":958497,"title":"","content":"My question is why would anyone want to go first edition? Just for the sin eaters? <br /> <br /> As stated earlier, blood talon crescent moon is your best bet. It's been a while, but I think that would focus your spiritual gifts in a combat centric roll. <br /> <br /> I could also be confusing it with apocalypse Fenrir crescent moons, who definitely focus on bringing the pain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T17:33:35-07:00","id":958512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957340-advice-on-character-build?p=958497#post958497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is why would anyone want to go first edition? Just for the sin eaters?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling 2e isn't out yet either. It may just be they like 1e better. I know I personally prefer 1e over 2e in some situations. Mostly because it's rules are a bit more flexable and easier to adjust if you want to change things up a bit.<br /> <br /> At least in my experiance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T17:57:05-07:00","id":958527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957340-advice-on-character-build?p=958497#post958497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is why would anyone want to go first edition?</div> </div> </div> </div> My group plays 1e because we have so many 1e books, it's going to be a bit costly to replace them not to mention a lot of these books don't exist in 2e as far as i can tell.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T18:01:41-07:00","id":958532,"title":"","content":"What I do is use 2nd edition rules and just add all the 1st edition fluff. Some gifts can be converted over fairly easily, but in no way am I not using anything from night horrors or signs of the moon. That stuffs all gold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}